  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN270.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">pakaṟkuṟikaṇ vantu nīṅkun talaimakaṉait tōḻi varaivu kaṭāyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">How the confidante urged HIM, who left after having come for the day tryst, for marriage.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN270.1">
        <l>iruṅkaḻi malarnta <anchor n="1"/>vaḷḷitaḻ <supplied>nī</supplied>lam</l>
        <l>pulāaṉ maṟukiṟ ciṟukuṭip pākkat</l>
        <l>tiṉamīṉ vēṭṭuvar ñāḻaloṭu milaiyu</l>
        <l>mellam pulampa nekiḻntaṉa tōḷē</l>
        <l>cēyiṟā<supplied>t tuḻa</supplied>nta nuraipitirp paṭu<supplied>ti</supplied>raip</l>
        <l>parāraip puṉṉai vāṅkuciṉait tōyuṅ</l>
        <l>kāṉalam peruntuṟai nōkki yiva<supplied>ḷē</supplied></l>
        <l>koycuvaṟ puravik kaivaṇ kōmā</l>
        <l>ṉa<supplied>ṟ</supplied>ṟērk kuṭṭuvaṉ kaḻumalat taṉṉa</l>
        <l>vammā mēṉit toṉṉalan tolaiyat</l>
        <l>tuñcāk kaṇṇa <supplied>ḷa</supplied>lamaru nīyē</l>
        <l>kaṭavuḷ maratta muṇ<supplied>mi</supplied>ṭai kuṭampai</l>
        <l>cēvaloṭu puṇa<supplied>rā</supplied>c ciṟukarum pēṭai</l>
        <l>yiṉṉā tuyaṅku<supplied>ṅ kaṅkulu</supplied></l>
        <l>nummū <supplied>ru</supplied>ḷḷutir nōkō yāṉē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="4ab">O gentle man of the lonely [seashore],</l>
        <l corresp="3">where the hunters for various fish wear with the Ñāḻal [blossoms]</l>
        <l corresp="1">blue [lotuses] with pointed petals that bloomed in the dark backwaters,</l>
        <l corresp="2">in [their] villages with small homes in fish-reeking streets,</l>
        <l corresp="4cd" rend="indent5">[her] shoulders are emaciated.</l>
        <l corresp="7">She, looking at the big ghat by the seashore grove,</l>
        <l corresp="5">where the coming waves with foaming spray that stirred red prawn</l>
        <l corresp="6">touch the bending branches of the large-trunked Puṉṉai trees,</l>
        <l corresp="11a-c">she is agitated, her eyes sleepless,</l>
        <l corresp="10">so that the old beauty is lost in [her] body, pretty [and] dark</l>
        <l corresp="9">like the Kaḻumalam of Kuṭṭuvaṉ with a good chariot,</l>
        <l corresp="8">the king liberal of hand, [his] horses with trimmed manes,</l>
        <l corresp="11d" rend="indent5">– you,</l>
        <l corresp="15ab">you should think of your village,</l>
        <l>all night, when the little dark she-bird</l>
        <l corresp="13f">not united with [its] male, is unpleasantly exhausted,</l>
        <l corresp="12">in the nest set close to the thorns of the god’s tree.</l>
        <l corresp="15cd" rend="indent5">Ah, I ache.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

